WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.509
Time and time again, Netflix has proven itself
to be the perfect place for audiences to discover

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:09.997
overlooked movies, and for those overlooked
movies to finally get some eyes on them.

00:00:09.997 --> 00:00:14.096
Perhaps it's due to the wider audience or
the ease of browsing for new flicks to watch,

00:00:14.096 --> 00:00:19.249
but either way, a lot of box office flops
and critical bombs have Netflix to thank for their viewership.

00:00:19.249 --> 00:00:25.963
One of those flops is the 2020 sci-fi action
movie Skylines, currently dominating Netflix's viewership charts.

00:00:25.963 --> 00:00:30.820
The dystopian adventure is actually the third
entry in the Skyline franchise, following

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.245
2010's Skyline and 2017's Beyond Skyline.

00:00:34.245 --> 00:00:39.360
Sadly, the trilogy got started on a less-than-ideal
note, with the 2010 original tanking at the

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.832
box office and receiving mostly poor reviews
from critics.

00:00:42.832 --> 00:00:48.150
However, Beyond Skyline rejected the sophomore
slump expectation and wound up earning pretty

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:52.677
solid reviews, even if audiences still weren't
totally on board with the franchise.

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:54.180
"Things are looking up, kid."

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.910
Skylines debuted in theaters and on Apple
TV in December 2020, but its arrival on Netflix

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.202
in March 2021 has breathed new life into the
movie.

00:01:03.202 --> 00:01:08.370
As of March 23, Skylines has remained in the
list of Netflix's top ten most-watched movies

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:13.307
in the U.S. for several days - something not
many other projects, film or otherwise, have achieved.

00:01:13.363 --> 00:01:17.850
Directed by Liam O'Donnell, who also wrote
the film's script, Skylines picks up where

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:22.860
the second film left off: now-grown-up resistance
leader Captain Rose Corley is leading a team

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:28.070
of elite mercenaries, including both humans
and bio-mechanical entities that were formerly

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.446
enslaved as soldiers.

00:01:29.446 --> 00:01:34.330
The end of Beyond Skylines saw Rose and her
team flying around the Moon, attacking other ships.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:38.630
At the start of Skylines, the human portion
of the crew is focused on battling the Harvester

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.034
mothership known as the Armada, which will
use its weapons to blow up Earth.

00:01:43.034 --> 00:01:47.460
Rose hits a crossroads when she realizes that
the only way she can defeat the Armada and

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.770
save Earth is to put one of her own ships
in the line of fire, a move that could only

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:53.831
result in everyone on the ship dying.

00:01:53.831 --> 00:01:57.860
She makes the difficult decision in order
to protect Earth, then disappears for half

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.458
a decade as she works through her guilt and
grief.

00:02:00.458 --> 00:02:04.979
When Rose emerges, living in London amongst
Pilot aliens and trying to keep herself hidden

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:07.316
from Leon, humanity has changed.

00:02:07.316 --> 00:02:13.161
A virus breaks out and turns into a pandemic,
affecting Pilots and anyone who has Pilot parts.

00:02:13.161 --> 00:02:17.950
It destroys not only the Pilots' bodies but
also their minds, causing them to revert back

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.700
to their original hostile selves.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.621
"The pilots are dying, Rose.

00:02:22.621 --> 00:02:25.184
What you saw today was only the beginning."

00:02:25.184 --> 00:02:29.170
It's up to Rose and her team to put an end
to the virus before it's too late.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.821
The group heads to the aliens' home planet
in an attempt to save the world.

00:02:32.821 --> 00:02:38.250
At the time of its release, Skylines didn't
blow people away - not critics and not general audiences.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.820
Some reviews were mostly negative and some
were rather glowing, but across the board,

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:47.040
critics felt that Skylines was kind of like
its title: a middle-of-the-road movie that

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.430
rests on the horizon line.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.640
Polygon's Tasha Robinson put it best when
she wrote in her review of the film,

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:57.330
"Skylines feels like the respectable thirtysomething
iteration of a familiar friend who used to

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.669
be a rowdy teen, then a reckless and wild
twentysomething.

00:03:00.669 --> 00:03:05.520
It's perfectly passable low-key science fiction,
almost certainly destined for a fast trip

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.360
to Netflix, where it can be taken up as an
amiable evening's viewing."

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:14.613
Netflix is exactly where Skylines ended up,
and subscribers are now singing the film's praises.

00:03:14.613 --> 00:03:15.917
One Twitter user wrote,

00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:20.260
"Skylines is honestly a good movie and I hope
y'all will watch it now that it's on Netflix

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.000
because it's soooo worth it and that it's
what the cast &amp; crew deserve!!"

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.839
Critic Matthew Essary even took the time to
share a six-tweet thread about Skylines' merits, writing in part,

00:03:29.839 --> 00:03:34.489
"I wanted to let you know that the incredibly
fun sci-fi sequel SKYLINES is on @netflix

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:37.189
starting today [March 18, 2021]!

00:03:37.189 --> 00:03:41.560
It joins the previous entry in the series,
BEYOND SKYLINE, on the services and these

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.592
two films form an excellent standalone sci-fi
tale.

00:03:44.592 --> 00:03:48.959
[...] I legitimately love SKYLINES and the
earlier BEYOND SKYLINE and I think you will too."

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:54.614
If you're in the mood for a fun, action-packed
adventure, Skylines is worth adding to your must-watch list.

